\section{MRI Pipeline - Full Technical Specification}

\subsection{Pre-processing Workflow}

Images were handled in a Singularity container (Ubuntu 22.04, Python 3.10, SimpleITK 2.x, TorchIO 0.19; global seed = 42).

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Auto-ROI selection}: Axial slices retained only if $\ge$ 50\% of voxels lay inside the sacro-iliac-joint (SIJ) bounding box generated by a coarse U-Net.
    \item \textbf{Signal-to-noise check}: Slices with in-plane SNR $<$ 15 were discarded.
    \item \textbf{Intensity correction}: N4 bias-field correction (shrink = 2, conv-threshold = $1 \times 10^{-7}$, max-iter = [50, 50, 30, 20]).
    \item \textbf{Spatial smoothing}: 3-D Gaussian filter $\sigma = 0.51$ mm (isotropic).
    \item \textbf{Resampling}: To $0.7 \times 0.7$ mm in-plane; slice thickness unchanged.
    \item \textbf{Cropping \& resizing}: Center-crop $224 \times 224$ and zero-pad if necessary.
    \item \textbf{Intensity normalisation}: z-score with ImageNet mean/std (0.485 / 0.229 per channel).
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Result}: 39 diagnostic slices from 8 subjects (6 AS, 2 HC).

\subsection{Feature Extraction \& Cross-Validation}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Backbone}: ResNet-18 pre-trained on ImageNet, all layers frozen.
    \item \textbf{Embedding}: average-pool Layer-4 activations $\rightarrow$ 512-dimensional vector per slice; mean across slices for subject-level representation.
    \item \textbf{Data augmentation} (TorchIO random 3-D): rotation $\pm10^\circ$, translation $\pm5$ px, Gaussian noise $\sigma = 0.01$, applied on-the-fly during training folds.
    \item \textbf{Feature filtering}:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Low-variance threshold = 0.01 (\texttt{sklearn VarianceThreshold}).
        \item ANOVA F-test: retain top $k = \min(50, n\_\text{features})$.
        \item Outlier pruning with Isolation Forest (contamination = 0.10, 200 trees, max-samples = 'auto').
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Classifier ensemble} (weighted-vote):
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Elastic-net logistic regression (C = 1.0, l1-ratio = 0.5)
        \item Pure L1 logistic regression (C = 0.5)
        \item Pure L2 logistic regression (C = 1.0)
        \item Balanced random forest (200 trees, max-depth = None, class\_weight = 'balanced')
        \item Linear SVM (C = 1.0, class\_weight = 'balanced')
        \item RBF-kernel SVM (C = 1.0, $\gamma$ = 'scale', class\_weight = 'balanced')
    \end{enumerate}
    Voting weights determined by inverse log-loss on training fold.
    \item \textbf{Cross-validation}: 12-fold leave-two-out (L2O-CV), each fold holding out 1 AS + 1 HC subject.
    \item \textbf{Probability post-processing}:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Polarity check: if fold AUROC $<$ 0.50, probabilities were flipped ($1 - p$).
        \item Temperature scaling on validation logits (grid-search $T \in [0.5, 5]$, step 0.05).
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Significance testing}: 1,000-iteration permutation test (class-label shuffle) $\rightarrow p = 0.017$.
    \item \textbf{Bootstrap CI}: 1,000 resamples, bias-corrected percentile method $\rightarrow$ subject-level AUROC 95\% CI 0.712–0.948.
    \item \textbf{Visual analytics}: t-SNE (perplexity = 5, 1,000 iter, learning-rate = 200) on 512-D embeddings; Grad-CAM fine-tune 3 epochs (Adam, LR = $1 \times 10^{-4}$, batch = 8) confirmed SIJ focus.
\end{itemize}
\clearpage

\section{Integration Strategy - Rationale and Hyper-parameters}

\subsection{Late-fusion Equation}
$$ P_{\text{ensemble}} = w_{\text{clin}} \times P_{\text{ClinicalNet}} + w_{\text{img}} \times P_{\text{ImagingNet}} $$
with $w_{\text{clin}} = w_{\text{img}} = 0.5$. Weights were fixed a-priori for transparency and to avoid optimising on the small imaging cohort; sensitivity analysis (weights 0.3–0.7) changed AUROC by $< 0.002$.

\subsection{Out-of-fold Probability Generation}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{ClinicalNet}: 5-fold stratified CV on the 4,254-sample balanced set; each validation fold's calibrated probabilities stored.
    \item \textbf{ImagingNet}: 12-fold L2O-CV; validation fold probabilities taken after temperature scaling.
    \item \textbf{Concatenated out-of-fold predictions} formed the training meta-vector for ensemble weight justification, but since equal weights performed within 0.1\% of an optimised logistic-stacker (and avoid over-fitting the 8-subject imaging set) the simple average was chosen.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Evaluation on Hold-out Set}
The independent hold-out comprised 10,383 encounters (prevalence $\approx 12\%$). Ensemble probabilities were obtained by passing:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Each encounter through the final ClinicalNet model (trained on full balanced set).
    \item Each MRI slice (if present) through ImagingNet; if no MRI, ImagingNet probability left as \texttt{NaN} and ensemble defaults to ClinicalNet (i.e. $P_{\text{ensemble}} = P_{\text{clinical}}$).
    \item Final AUROC = 0.941, ECE = 0.168, sensitivity = 99.5\% at threshold 0.62 (Youden).
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Software \& Reproducibility}
All code is version-controlled (Git tag v1.2.0) and containerised (Docker 24.0, CUDA 11.8). Re-run instructions with \texttt{make reproduce-all} generate identical results on Linux/x86-64 with GPU $\ge$6 GB.
\clearpage

